  "notes": "{徐行|じょこう} refers to driving or moving at a reduced speed, typically for safety.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {徐行|じょこう}する: to go slowly, to drive slowly\n- {徐行|じょこう}{区間|くかん}: slow zone\n- {徐行|じょこう}{運転|うんてん}: slow driving\n- {徐行|じょこう}の{標識|ひょうしき}: slow sign\n\nTRAFFIC SIGNS:\n- {徐行|じょこう} appears on road signs indicating areas where slow speed is required\n- Common near schools, construction zones, and sharp curves\n\nLEGAL DEFINITION:\n- In Japanese traffic law, {徐行|じょこう} means driving at a speed slow enough to stop immediately if needed",
